        <div class="allocation-grid"><article class="card padded"><h3>Planning allowances</h3><p>Configurable estimates for each reported affected person, for the requested planning period.</p><form @submit.prevent="w.saveBaseline"><label>Drinking water (L / person / day)<input v-model.number="w.drinkingBaseline" type="number" min="0.5" max="30" step="0.1" required :disabled="w.disabled"></label><label>Food preparation (L / person / day)<input v-model.number="w.cookingBaseline" type="number" min="0" max="30" step="0.1" required :disabled="w.disabled"></label><div class="formula">Total: {{ w.fmt(w.drinkingBaseline + w.cookingBaseline) }} L / person / day</div><label>Reason for changing the allowances<textarea v-model="w.baselineReason" minlength="5" placeholder="Record the planning context and basis" required :disabled="w.disabled" /></label><p v-if="w.formError" class="form-error" role="alert">{{ w.formError }}</p><button class="secondary" :disabled="w.disabled || !w.baselineReason.trim()">Apply allowances</button></form><p class="muted">These are planning assumptions, not universal medical quotas. Climate, diet, age, and local conditions can change needs. They exclude bathing and other non-food household uses.</p><hr><label>Dispatch budget (liters)<input v-model.number="w.budget" type="number" min="0" :max="w.available(w.s)" step="1" :disabled="w.disabled"></label><p v-if="!w.budgetValid" class="form-error" role="alert">Enter a whole-liter budget from zero to the currently available stock.</p><button type="button" class="text-button" :disabled="w.disabled" @click="w.resetAllocation">Use current available stock</button><p class="muted">Available inventory: {{ w.fmt(w.available(w.s)) }} L. Set the budget to what can be dispatched in this planning run.</p><hr><h3>How shares are calculated</h3><p class="formula">Affected people × (drinking + food-preparation allowance) × planning days − local potable water × planning days − actual assistance − active commitments</p><p>Scarce stock is shared in proportion to each verified request’s eligible unmet need. Whole-liter rounding uses the largest remainder, with request ID breaking ties.</p><p>Elevated urgency stays visible for human review. It does not silently change the proportional calculation.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><div class="card-heading"><div><h3>Recommended potable water distribution</h3><p>{{ w.fmt(w.proposed) }} L recommended from {{ w.fmt(w.eligibleNeed) }} L eligible need</p></div><span class="badge teal">Explainable</span></div>
